I tried to create a minimal agent with the latest package, I believe these are the required steps:

1. Create new WebAPI dotnet project

```bash
dotnet new webapi -o MyFirstAgent
cd MyFirstAgent
```

2. Add NuGet package

```bash
dotnet add package Microsoft.Agents.Hosting.AspNetCore --version 0.2.287-alpha
```

3. Update Program.cs

```cs
using Microsoft.Agents.Builder.App;
using Microsoft.Agents.Core.Models;
using Microsoft.Agents.Hosting.AspNetCore;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Services.AddControllers();
builder.Services.AddHttpClient();
builder.AddAgent(sp =>
{
    var agent = new AgentApplication(new AgentApplicationOptions());
    agent.OnActivity(ActivityTypes.Message, async (turnContext, turnState, cancellationToken) =>
    {
        await turnContext.SendActivityAsync(MessageFactory.Text($"Echo: {turnContext.Activity.Text}"), cancellationToken);
    });
    return agent;
});

var app = builder.Build();
//app.UseHttpsRedirection();
app.MapGet("/", () => "Microsoft Agents SDK Sample");
app.MapControllers().AllowAnonymous();

app.Run();
```
> this quickstart is configured for Anonymous authentication, before deploying you must configure authentication Link TBD

4. Run and Test

```bash
dotnet run
``` 

In Bot Framework Emulator, open a new Bot using the post shown in the output of `dotnet run`
